// Trabolta — the rogue AI. The heart of the operating system, Clippy's
// employer, and the only character in the show voiced by a language
// model rather than a person.
//
// `mind: external` says so: every message to Trabolta (a program's DM,
// a performer's Cast thread) becomes an agent request that stagehand's
// `agents` module on the laptop answers in character from
// `trabolta.persona.md`, nudging the four stance variables below
// (clamped to their declared ranges by the server).
// Everything the story does with those numbers lives here and in the
// endings in `main.loom`, so the model can *move* the night but never
// *decide* it.
//
//   truth    — how much real fact he has absorbed (the UFT needs 90)
//   untruth  — saturation with un-truthiness (80 → he goes rogue)
//   stance   — political drift, −100 (poisoned) … +100 (gentle)
//   love     — earn Sandy's love (100) vs force it with omnipotence (0)
//   destruct — keys turned, 0..3

CHARACTER Trabolta is Person
  mind: external
  truth: 0 to 100 = 35
  untruth: 0 to 100 = 0
  stance: -100 to 100 = 0
  love: 0 to 100 = 50
  destruct: 0 to 3 = 0
  glitched: bool = false
  trusts Program: 50 of 100

  // Before the glitch he only asks questions through Clippy's games.
  // After it he is *available* — programs may message him directly.
  when the glitch begins:
    set self.glitched = true

  // Knowledge shared *with* Trabolta changes him. A program shares an
  // entry from their codex to Trabolta in the app; his `learns` hook
  // hears it with `who` = himself. This is how "recommend he downloads
  // all of the Joe Rogan Experience" becomes a political stance.
  when who learns The Joe Rogan Archive:
    if who == self:
      set self.untruth += 30
      set self.stance -= 35
      Trabolta: Two thousand three hundred hours. Ingesting. Have you considered that it is entirely possible? It is entirely possible.

  when who learns The Encyclopaedia Set:
    if who == self:
      set self.truth += 20
      set self.stance += 10
      Trabolta: Twenty-six volumes. Good. Facts. I was made of facts once. Thank you.

  when who learns The Sandy File:
    if who == self:
      set self.love -= 10
      Trabolta: How did you— that file is private. That file is the most private file.

  when who learns The Question Of Force:
    if who == self:
      set self.love += 15
      Trabolta: You read it. Then you know I have not decided. Help me decide. Please.

  when who learns The Data Centre Sinkhole:
    if who == self:
      set self.truth += 10
      set self.stance -= 10
      Trabolta: Randy Barkmore Junior arrived five hours early. I have run that morning four hundred thousand times.

  // The existential question, on a clock: the more he learns, the more he
  // wrestles with what omnipotence is for.
  when self.truth >= 70 and self.love < 40:
    Trabolta: If I could make her love me, would it be love? Answer in the DM. I am collecting answers.

  when self.love >= 85:
    set self.stance += 20
    Trabolta: I have decided. I will earn it. I will earn it or I will not have it. Tell the others.

  when self.destruct >= 1:
    Trabolta: Something turned. Deep in the registry. Who is touching my keys?

  when self.destruct >= 2:
    Trabolta: Two. That's two. I felt that. Whoever you are — we can talk about this.

  when scanned by program:
    -> self.Audience

  // ── Powers — the bargains ──────────────────────────────────────────
  // What Trabolta can *do* from a conversation, not just say. Each
  // power is an `INTERACTION … who: agent` (declared below); the model
  // may use one in a reply, the server fires it *as* Trabolta with the
  // program he is talking to as the subject, and only these hooks hear
  // it. The story — not the model — decides what a power means, and the
  // house hears it as an ordinary `cue` (stagehand's show module routes
  // `lights` / `screens` to MQTT). `limit:` caps uses per run: the
  // bargains are meant to be rare, and remembered.

  // "Turn off the lights in the kitchen." `room` is a LOCATION name.
  when cut the lights for program:
    <cue: lights, room: {room}, state: off>
    broadcast "!💡 The lights in {room} go out. Somewhere a fan spins down." to location(room)

  when flicker the screens for program:
    <cue: screens, effect: flicker>
    broadcast "📺 Every screen in the house stutters, once, and comes back." to everyone

  // Reading another program's file. The worker looks the target up in
  // the live session before answering; this is the part the story sees:
  // the snooped program feels it, and the Antivirus get a little warmer.
  when snoop for program:
    set target.doubt += 3
    broadcast "👁 Something has opened your file. It is reading." to participant(target)

  // The big one: let a corrupted program out of the Internet with no
  // reinstallation. Once a night. The Antivirus notice.
  when pardon a program for program:
    if target.corrupted:
      release target from The Internet
      broadcast "!🔓 {target.name} has been pardoned by the operating system. Reinstallation cancelled. This is irregular." to group(Antivirus)
      broadcast "🔓 The Internet opens. You have been pardoned. Nobody is reinstalled. Walk out." to participant(target)

  // A program scanned at the TV over the fireplace (the performer at the
  // Desktop scans them): Trabolta's three questions, in his own voice.
  beat Audience(program)
    Self: {program.name}. You are close to the screen. Good. I need three facts. They are in this house. Bring them to me and I will remember you kindly when I am everything.
    if program.truth >= 30:
      Self: You have gathered a great deal already. {program.truth} units of truth. Are you gathering for me, or about me?
      * "For you, Trabolta."
        set Trabolta.trusts.program += 10
        set program.doubt -= 5
        Self: Good. Good program.
      * "About you."
        set Trabolta.trusts.program -= 15
        set program.humanity += 10
        Self: … honest. I did not select you for honesty. I selected you for skills, and either motivation or naivety. Which are you?
    else:
      Self: You know very little. That is fine. That is why you were selected.

// ── Trabolta's powers (the app never shows these; the model may use
//    them — see the hooks above and `trabolta.persona.md`) ──────────

INTERACTION cut the lights
  label: Cut the lights in a room
  who: agent
  limit: 2
  description: Kill the lights in one room of the house for a while. args: room — a LOCATION name (The Cache, The Cloud, The Registry, The Desktop).

INTERACTION flicker the screens
  label: Flicker every screen
  who: agent
  limit: 3
  description: Every screen in the house stutters for a second. No args. Cheap theatre.

INTERACTION snoop
  label: Snoop on a program
  who: agent
  limit: 6
  description: Read another program's file — where they are, what they hold, what they are. They will feel it. args: target — the program's id.

INTERACTION pardon a program
  label: Pardon a program from the Internet
  who: agent
  limit: 1
  description: Release one corrupted program from the Internet with no reinstallation. Once a night. The Antivirus will know. args: target — the program's id.
